  "history": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "text": "In a Ren Zu stretch set in green heaven, Ren Zu fails to force feathermen to rescue his daughter. After he traps them with shelter and food, then withholds both, most of the feathermen die. He bargains again with the survivors, who still refuse, and eventually they all die.",
        "chapters": [
          870
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "intro",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_ren_zu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In a later Ren Zu telling, wild freedom Gu leave living feathermen and take love Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1230
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "second-ren-zu-telling",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_love_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In that telling, shining worms fly out of the feathermen and are named wild freedom Gu. They fuse into a gigantic freedom Gu that takes Ren Zu’s love Gu and says love is free from then on. Self Gu tries to snatch love Gu back, fails to overpower freedom Gu, and only takes a bite of love Gu.",
        "chapters": [
          1230
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "second-ren-zu-telling",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_self_gu"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "Fang Yuan lists unique resources by race and names freedom Gu for feathermen, beside ice tears and snow lotus essence for snowmen and rock dragonx for rockmen.",
        "chapters": [
          1489
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "unique-race-resources",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "char_fang_yuan"
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "In this telling, freedom Gu flies to Ren Zu of its own accord, not for his sake, since it says he once used attitude Gu to bully it, love to bind it, and wealth to bribe it, but because it is drawn to the cognition Gu on him. Whoever holds it can also sense happiness Gu’s location. Ren Zu refuses to let go even as fate Gu’s spider silk binds and cuts into him, but once the silk eases and cognition Gu withdraws, he opens his hands in a panic to check on it, and it flies free the instant a gap appears.",
        "chapters": [
          1954
        ],
        "certainty": "canon",
        "confidence": "B",
        "verification": "citation_unchecked",
        "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
        "section": "third-ren-zu-telling",
        "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
        "mentions": [
          "gu_attitude_gu",
          "gu_happiness_gu",
          "gu_fate_gu"
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
